    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0427" n="387" xml:id="pg387"/>

                <head>119. Instruction From the Department of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Missions<anchor n="1" xml:id="d119-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">CA–10538</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1959-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1959</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Authorization of Arms Shipments to Caribbean Area</item>
                </list>
                <p>In order to provide more detailed guidance than that contained in Circular
                    Telegram 1141 of April 3, 1959<anchor n="2" xml:id="d119-f2"/> respecting
                    consideration by the Department of applications for licenses to export military
                    equipment to the Caribbean area, a memorandum was recently prepared in the
                    Department setting forth the more important elements of the current practice
                    respecting this matter. This memorandum, a copy of which is enclosed, has been
                    distributed to officers of the Bureau of Inter-American Affairs and the Office
                    of Munitions Control for their guidance in considering export license
                    applications.</p>
                <p>Comments of Embassies to which this Instruction is sent for action are requested
                    respecting the guidelines set out in this memorandum.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Dillon</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d119-a1.xml" xpointer="d119-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d119-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d119-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 413.118/6–359. Confidential. Drafted
                    by Little, and approved by Snow. Sent to Bogotá, Caracas, Ciudad Trujillo,
                    Guatemala, Habana, Managua, Mexico, Panamá, Port-au-Prince, San José, San
                    Salvador, and Tegucigalpa; repeated to Asunción, Bonn, Brussels, Buenos Aires,
                    La Paz, Lima, London, Madrid, Montevideo, Oslo, Ottawa, Paris, Quito, Rome, Rio
                    de Janeiro, Santiago, Stockholm, and The Hague.</p>
            </note>
